# 0.13.2 (#44): notes are laid out at the height they're drawn at. In this grid the middle row
# holds only notes, which wrap onto more lines than their length suggests. Look for: the board
# tall enough for everything, the arrow's lane under the screens (not across "Below"), and in
# the measured image, the boxes on the drawn frames.
# measured
board "Grid drift" layout=grid columns=2
  screen phone "Top" #top
    button "Next" primary #next
  note "WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL"
  note "WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL WARNING: MANDATORY REVIEW WINDOW MUST MATCH WORKFLOW WWW MMM QA APPROVAL"
  note "Short"
  screen phone "Below" #below
    button "Done" #done
  flow next -> done "go"
